join Gogo (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Gogo: I'll tell you what I know, which isn't advice. It's just what happened to me.
Gogo: I was not born in this village. I married into it. I could have left, after — more than once, if I'm honest.
Gogo: I stayed because I kept finding one more reason. And then one day I noticed I had run out of counting them, because it was simply where I lived.
- How do you know when that's happened?
	Hope: How do you know when that's happened?
	Gogo: You don't, while it's happening. You only know afterward, when someone asks you to leave and the question feels wrong in your mouth before you've even answered it.
	Gogo: That's all I have for you. Not an answer. Just company while you find your own.
